# Trivy CVE Ignore List
# ====================
#
# This file lists CVEs that Trivy should skip during scanning.
# The dependency-gate job in .github/workflows/security.yml uses this file
# to allow merge even when a known CVE has no available fix or is not applicable.
#
# EXCEPTION PROCESS:
# 1. A CRITICAL/HIGH CVE blocks the merge via the dependency-gate job.
# 2. If the CVE has no fix available or is not exploitable in our context,
#    open a follow-up issue to track it, then add it here with justification.
# 3. Each entry MUST include: CVE ID, justification, tracking issue, and expiry date.
# 4. Review this file monthly — remove entries once a fix is released.
#
# FORMAT:
#   # <justification> (tracking: #NNN, expires: YYYY-MM-DD)
#   CVE-YYYY-NNNNN
#
# EXAMPLES (uncommented when needed):
#   # No fix available in current OpenSlide release (tracking: #000, expires: 2026-06-01)
#   CVE-2024-00000
#
#   # Not exploitable: requires local filesystem access we don't expose (tracking: #000, expires: 2026-06-01)
#   CVE-2024-99999
